WEBVTT

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:37.530
Shin, watch yourself.

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:38.630
I'm fine!

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:41.120
Jun, Yuki, be careful.

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:43.600
Don't worry!

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:44.400
Look ou-

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:49.440
I'm first!

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.410
Me, too!

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:55.710
Huh?

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:57.050
It's not there?

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:06.790
Welcome back, Ryo-niichan!

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.790
Welcome back, oniichan!

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:13.700
I'm back.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:29.020
Oh ware izukoe
Oh, where am I?

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:34.980
Oh ware yobukoe
Oh, the voice that's calling me

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:38.490
umetsukusu jouhou
Immersing information

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:42.860
ikigurushii kono joukyou
This suffocating situation

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:47.140
jibun ga inai
I'm not here

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:50.640
kono sekai no bousou
The world is going out of control

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:54.410
tada musekinin ni toubou
Run away irresponsibly

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:57.680
dokoe ikuno
Where am I going?

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:00.150
Huriyamanu ameni
The never-ending rain

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:03.950
zubunure oitekareta kokoro ga
Soak the neglected heart

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:08.860
kuzure yuku chokuzen no koe wo kike
Listen to the voices before it collapses

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:14.730
sasayakana kizunade ii
I'm fine with the subtle connection

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:20.670
sotto anata wo dakishimeru kara
I will hold you gently

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:32.180
kasaneta inochi ga
yukkurito ima kokyuu shite iru
The overlapped souls breathe slowly

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:35.950
sobani iruyo
"I'll be by your side."

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:41.720
Oh ware izukoe
Oh, where am I?

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:49.320
Oh ware yobukoe
Oh, the voice that's calling me

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:02.100
Ow!

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:06.170
I bet you use up all the bandages at home yourself.

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:18.290
How was Kyoto?

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:20.420
I think I got 80% of it.

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:23.730
I'm applying for the second half, just in case.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:26.900
Well, not just the entry exam, but the area itself.

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:30.060
Wasn't it a good place?

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:34.940
Yeah. I didn't really have time
to enjoy the scenery, though.

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:39.450
Once you're settled over there,
we should all come visit.

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:41.680
Yeah! I wanna go!

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:45.490
By then, I'm sure we'll be done with our work, too.

00:03:45.890 --> 00:03:48.090
I haven't gotten accepted yet...

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:49.490
Ryo-niichan.

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:52.420
I wanna play horse, too.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:55.420
Giddy up!

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.260
Please!

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:03.630
Shin-niichan...

00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:08.140
You're too slow.

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:25.780
Niicha...You're going too fast!

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.090
Eiko-neechan.

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:38.370
Niichan, that wasn't nice!

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:43.300
If you're interested...

00:04:44.310 --> 00:04:45.780
That's a big one.

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:46.940
It looks fresh.

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:51.090
My father went fishing with
a patient from the clinic.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:52.710
They caught a lot more than usual.

00:04:53.050 --> 00:04:54.780
Thank you. We'll take it.

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:56.750
You'll have dinner with us, right?

00:04:57.890 --> 00:04:58.950
Oh... yes.

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:03.750
Ryo, Eiko-chan is here!

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.370
Eiko-oneechan!

00:05:09.770 --> 00:05:11.500
Good evening, Yuki-chan.

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:16.630
Now, help me make dinner.
Eiko-chan will be with us tonight.

00:05:16.910 --> 00:05:17.900
Yay!

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:20.610
I'll help!

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:24.640
Helping!

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:28.850
What?

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:33.360
What is it? Come in. It's cold out.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:37.290
Y-yeah... How'd it go? Your exam.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:39.930
Not bad. How about you?

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:42.630
Um... Okay, I guess.

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:44.170
Cool.

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:49.500
H-hey...

00:05:51.980 --> 00:05:53.350
About tomorrow...

00:05:53.350 --> 00:05:54.440
Do you have time?

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:05.190
We won't be coming back.

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:08.360
We were hoping you'd realize that someday.

00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:14.160
...Even for you, there are lines you
mustn't cross, Dr. Komatsubara.

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:21.730
We lost sight of that during our
research of the human psyche and mind.

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:25.140
Since the incident, you've gotten even more-

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:29.310
No, perhaps... your-

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:31.980
Your true objective is to...

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:36.880
The very thing a human should never do.

00:06:39.890 --> 00:06:41.450
I brought you coffee.

00:06:42.530 --> 00:06:44.960
Getting pressed by your editor again?

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:46.430
Yeah...

00:06:47.030 --> 00:06:49.030
Are they all asleep?

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:51.970
Yeah, they must be tired from playing.

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:53.030
I see.

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:55.970
Is that the last page?

00:06:56.480 --> 00:06:58.640
Yes. It's almost done.

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:03.180
The title, A Whale's Feather,
is Yuki's protective charm, right?

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:06.310
I looked it up, but didn't find it anywhere.

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:08.880
Ryo.

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:12.550
Can you make some time tomorrow?

00:07:13.130 --> 00:07:15.120
I have something I need to talk to you about.

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:16.320
Honey...

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:32.670
Want some juice?

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:38.880
Here.

00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:40.450
Thanks.

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:42.350
What are you doing?

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:45.490
It's a secret.

00:07:46.790 --> 00:07:48.020
Oh?

00:07:49.260 --> 00:07:51.930
I feel bad for Eiko-chan.

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:54.400
At least she got to go to the theme park.

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:57.990
You don't get it, huh?

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:03.910
It's been a while since the three
of us spent some time like this.

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:05.000
That's true.

00:08:05.180 --> 00:08:09.170
Probably not since Ryo reached the age of reason.

00:08:09.850 --> 00:08:13.010
We couldn't be there for you for a long time.

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:21.460
You know your mother and
I had a different job before.

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:22.860
Yeah.

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:26.560
We want to talk to you about that time.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:29.530
And about the future.

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:36.380
Wait, Jun-kun, Yuki-chan!

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:39.510
Shin-kun, we have to make
sure those two don't get lost.

00:08:39.510 --> 00:08:42.880
Eiko-neechan, let's go ride the Tea Cups!

00:08:45.220 --> 00:08:46.050
Ugh!

00:08:49.490 --> 00:08:50.720
I feel sick.

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:53.490
You spun it way too fast.

00:09:02.170 --> 00:09:03.300
Eiko-neechan.

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:07.800
You actually wanted to
come with Ryo-niichan, huh?

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:09.810
Oh, please.

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:13.910
You won't see Ryo-niichan
anymore once he goes to Kyoto.

00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:17.740
...Which ride do you wanna go on next?

00:09:19.690 --> 00:09:20.810
I want that.

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:26.980
I can't forget the last time I saw her eyes.

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:43.240
We're thinking of bringing charges against them.

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:48.440
This is also your mother's and my confession.

00:09:49.250 --> 00:09:49.940
So...

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:53.140
We won't be able to come back to you guys.

00:09:56.090 --> 00:09:57.350
We're sorry, Ryo.

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:05.070
We sacrificed your childhood,
then ran away from our sins.

00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:08.260
And, again, we're doing this to you.

00:10:10.870 --> 00:10:11.860
We're so sorry.

00:10:12.910 --> 00:10:14.170
Shhh, okay?

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:16.500
Where's Shin?

00:10:16.980 --> 00:10:18.000
The bathroom.

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:19.940
He said he has a stomachache.

00:10:20.920 --> 00:10:22.080
Which bathroom?

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:22.910
That way!

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:26.010
What kind of prank is this?

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:32.790
He said he was gonna bring Ryo-niichan...

00:10:32.790 --> 00:10:36.960
He told us to keep it a secret until they got here.

00:10:56.420 --> 00:10:57.910
Ayane...chan...

00:11:17.870 --> 00:11:19.670
Eiko-oneechan!

00:12:06.890 --> 00:12:07.580
Eiko!

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:09.850
Where are Jun and Yuki!?

00:12:10.190 --> 00:12:12.250
They're in the treatment room, but...

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:16.460
Watch Shin for me.

00:12:23.370 --> 00:12:24.300
Shin-kun?

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:32.540
I can't understand what you're saying.

00:12:34.820 --> 00:12:42.310
Just as I said; we will transplant a part of your
sister's brain to treat your brother's injury.

00:12:42.860 --> 00:12:44.090
How could?

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:47.560
The history of transplants is older than you think.

00:12:47.560 --> 00:12:52.170
There are still many logical and legal issues, but...

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:55.160
Is my sister... is Yuki still alive?

00:12:55.370 --> 00:13:00.570
Unfortunately, it's just a matter
of time. Her injury is too severe.

00:13:00.570 --> 00:13:02.770
Even your brother will be...

00:13:04.410 --> 00:13:07.720
Brains in their development stages are flexible.

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:11.550
There's enough chance of it being compatible
and resulting in complete recovery.

00:13:11.550 --> 00:13:17.150
It's either you lose both of them,
or save at least your brother.

00:13:18.160 --> 00:13:20.650
You're still fortunate.

00:13:22.200 --> 00:13:23.420
Where are your parents?

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:25.620
Not here.

00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:31.300
We don't have time. Please, we need
your signature indicating approval.

00:13:43.880 --> 00:13:44.540
Ryo!

00:13:45.990 --> 00:13:46.880
...How did it go?

00:13:48.960 --> 00:13:50.790
Shin, let's go home.

00:13:51.230 --> 00:13:52.750
But he still needs-

00:13:55.630 --> 00:13:58.030
Ryo! What's wrong with Shin-kun?

00:13:58.730 --> 00:13:59.930
What happened?

00:14:11.180 --> 00:14:13.110
Is anything else hurt?

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:24.120
(Missing Persons)

00:14:24.190 --> 00:14:25.990
Please, don't lose hope.

00:14:25.990 --> 00:14:27.890
Tell us your son's characteristics.

00:14:33.370 --> 00:14:35.600
Ito, switch with Saeki.

00:14:35.870 --> 00:14:38.640
They seemed to have some
difficulties handling him.

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:41.900
Yeah... He said he saw a monster that day.

00:14:43.410 --> 00:14:46.970
Poor thing. It must be the
shock from losing his family.

00:14:48.620 --> 00:14:50.050
Anyway, you should get some rest.

00:14:50.580 --> 00:14:54.040
Your wife... and your daughter, also...

00:14:54.690 --> 00:14:59.250
Yeah, but if I don't stay busy,
I feel like I'll go out of my mind.

00:15:13.110 --> 00:15:14.970
Shin... You're gonna catch a cold.

00:15:24.550 --> 00:15:25.610
They were killed.

00:15:26.220 --> 00:15:27.350
By me.

00:15:27.620 --> 00:15:28.020
No!

00:15:29.390 --> 00:15:30.150
No!

00:15:32.130 --> 00:15:32.920
Shin!

00:15:44.100 --> 00:15:46.070
It's time for his check up.

00:15:46.070 --> 00:15:47.270
May I come in?

00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:53.240
Hold on...

00:15:53.610 --> 00:15:57.140
That boy... Seems to display different
symptoms than normal apathy victims.

00:16:00.820 --> 00:16:02.950
Partial memory removal?

00:16:03.420 --> 00:16:08.060
Not removing, but rather,
covering it up with hypnotherapy.

00:16:08.060 --> 00:16:12.570
Unless he receives a strong shock
or is under high intermittent stress,

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:18.900
as long as he lives a normal life,
the memory will not resurface.

00:16:20.170 --> 00:16:24.610
Before the procedure, I'd like to hear about
the part of his memory you want buried.

00:16:26.110 --> 00:16:28.670
What happened that day?

00:16:30.520 --> 00:16:32.920
I don't think you will believe me.

00:16:33.450 --> 00:16:37.320
What if I said I knew what kind of
research your parents were involved in?

00:16:38.730 --> 00:16:41.350
Kanzato Shigeru and Haruka...

00:16:41.900 --> 00:16:44.830
They're known as picture book writers,

00:16:44.900 --> 00:16:51.800
but they were also promising individuals
in neuroanatomy and psychophysics.

00:16:53.670 --> 00:16:55.900
They both regret their past.

00:16:56.310 --> 00:16:57.500
Did you see it, too?

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:02.040
Maybe we're not supposed to forget.

00:17:02.480 --> 00:17:06.040
Then Shin-kun will never smile again.

00:17:17.770 --> 00:17:19.430
Just like she used to be...

00:17:21.670 --> 00:17:22.770
This is Kanzato.

00:17:22.770 --> 00:17:24.290
She's... Ayane-chan is!

00:17:41.490 --> 00:17:42.220
Stop...

00:17:43.460 --> 00:17:44.420
Stop!

00:17:47.430 --> 00:17:48.090
Ryo...

00:17:49.430 --> 00:17:51.330
Please, take care of...

00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:55.360
Ryo...niichan?

00:17:55.740 --> 00:17:56.400
Shin!

00:17:59.210 --> 00:18:00.140
Dad...

00:18:00.940 --> 00:18:02.030
Don't look!

00:18:03.810 --> 00:18:05.870
Mom!

00:18:47.620 --> 00:18:49.590
Go away...

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:53.850
I don't want this!

00:19:18.320 --> 00:19:19.840
Let's process the discharge summary.

00:19:28.300 --> 00:19:29.500
Ryo-niichan!

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:31.020
Ryo-oniichan.

00:19:43.310 --> 00:19:44.400
Ryo-niichan!

00:19:59.030 --> 00:20:00.520
It's time to say goodbye, Shin.

00:20:12.540 --> 00:20:13.770
Oniichan.

00:20:14.370 --> 00:20:16.340
Promise to play horse with me again.

00:21:01.520 --> 00:21:04.980
Kanzato Shigeru Kanzato Haruka
Kanzato Yuki

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:09.060
Ito Mieko
Ito Yuuna

00:21:16.240 --> 00:21:18.030
Morimoto Kanaru

00:21:23.940 --> 00:21:25.610
Instead of the boy...

00:21:26.910 --> 00:21:28.780
You got your future.

00:21:52.240 --> 00:21:57.610
Itsukara yume miru koto
When did I start pretending
like I didn't dream of anything?

00:21:57.610 --> 00:22:03.650
Wasureta huri wo shitetan darou
When did I start pretending
like I didn't dream of anything?

00:22:03.650 --> 00:22:09.960
Chiisana mado akeru yuuki mo naku
With no courage to open a small
window, I waited for a miracle

00:22:09.960 --> 00:22:15.260
kiseki wo matteta
With no courage to open a small
window, I waited for a miracle

00:22:15.260 --> 00:22:25.310
ushinau mono nado nakatta anohi no yona
I'm not as innocent as I used to be in
the days when I had nothing to lose

00:22:25.310 --> 00:22:30.640
mujakisa wa mou naikedo
I'm not as innocent as I used to be in
the days when I had nothing to lose

00:22:30.640 --> 00:22:36.880
namida wo nugutta ato niwa
After wiping away the tears

00:22:36.880 --> 00:22:42.760
atarashii jibun ni deaeru
I'll be able to meet a new self

00:22:42.760 --> 00:22:42.790
Even if I lose everything

00:22:42.790 --> 00:22:46.690
subete wo nakushitemo
mitsuke rareru monoga arukara
Even if I lose everything

00:22:46.690 --> 00:22:52.900
subete wo nakushitemo
mitsuke rareru monoga arukara
There are still some things to discover

00:22:52.900 --> 00:22:58.710
kesenai kizumo itsuka
Even the scars that remain

00:22:58.710 --> 00:23:06.010
watashi rashii hokori ni dekiru
will someday become my pride

00:23:10.850 --> 00:23:13.820
Ordinary brothers.

00:23:13.820 --> 00:23:16.860
An ordinary family.

00:23:16.860 --> 00:23:19.930
An ordinary lover.

00:23:19.930 --> 00:23:23.700
An ordinary sight.

00:23:23.700 --> 00:23:26.670
I didn't know anything.

00:23:26.670 --> 00:23:31.140
Now I look at the world where nothing happened.

00:23:31.140 --> 00:23:34.170
I wish for this to last forever.

00:23:34.170 --> 00:23:38.200
This is how we were supposed to live.
